{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview","id":1514964,"title":"Garou-Forms plus Frenzy Rules - W5 Preview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-14T09:07:21-07:00","id":1514964,"title":"Garou-Forms plus Frenzy Rules - W5 Preview","content":"<div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1498\" height=\"959\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/pAiCSaT.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/pAiCSaT.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/pAiCSaT.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"1500\" height=\"958\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/LSjX19H.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/LSjX19H.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/LSjX19H.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> Instead of me listing any thoughts, I just have this to say: <b>The char-sheet we saw last week was not only from a playtest but from a previous build of the game!</b> <b>The char-sheet actually doesn't reflect what the final game is like... </b><br /> <br /> Why...?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:30:15-07:00","id":1514969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview#post1514964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Instead of me listing any thoughts, I just have this to say: <b>The char-sheet we saw last week was not only from a playtest but from a previous build of the game!</b> <b>The char-sheet actually doesn't reflect what the final game is like... </b><br /> <br /> Why...?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is that said?<br /> <br /> As for the previews themselves, given how goddamn common frenzy is going to be, getting out of it is way harder than it should be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:40:33-07:00","id":1514971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514969#post1514969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is that said?<br /> <br /> As for the previews themselves, given how goddamn common frenzy is going to be, getting out of it is way harder than it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, here we get additional info in that you can extend your Crinos-form indefinitely without risking Frenzy as long as you're killing something each turn. And the Lupus form mentions a potential 2-dice-bonus for Stealth and Survival. Why wouldn't you list that on Form-overview on the char-sheet...? There is room for it after all.<br /> <br /> As for Frenzy, yeah... seems like they're focusing on making it a real &quot;struggle&quot; to deal with your Rage.<br /> <br /> But then it also mentions how certain Gifts and other abilities can also end your Frenzy... while also saying that you can't use Gifts while in Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T09:55:58-07:00","id":1514972,"title":"","content":"&gt;Hispo<br /> &gt;Dire Wolf<br /> <br /> I realize that this is perhaps the least of the game's sins, but it still makes me want to [SCREAMS EXTERNALLY].<br /> <br /> Dire wolves were about as related to timber wolves as dholes or African painted dogs, which is to say, not particularly closely. They were also not nearly as large as the giant depictions that have been spawned by that one chart transposition from the AD&amp;D 2e Monstrous Compendium, which switched their size with that of worgs (check the 1e MM; dire wolves are Size M). Here, I'd hope this wouldn't be repeated again.<br /> <br /> (Also, they were unique to the Americas, and primarily North America. Not anywhere else. You find a lot of their remains in the LaBrea tar pits, actually.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:04:28-07:00","id":1514975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514972#post1514972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Hispo<br /> &gt;Dire Wolf<br /> <br /> I realize that this is perhaps the least of the game's sins, but it still makes me want to [SCREAMS EXTERNALLY].<br /> <br /> Dire wolves were about as related to timber wolves as dholes or African painted dogs, which is to say, not particularly closely. They were also not nearly as large as the giant depictions that have been spawned by that one chart transposition from the AD&amp;D 2e Monstrous Compendium, which switched their size with that of worgs (check the 1e MM; dire wolves are Size M). Here, I'd hope this wouldn't be repeated again.<br /> <br /> (Also, they were unique to the Americas, and primarily North America. Not anywhere else. You find a lot of their remains in the LaBrea tar pits, actually.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, they still keep saying lupus could be mistaken for a dog and says the same with hispo.<br /> <br /> Once more, even if you haven't seen a wolf before you'd still notice how HUEG that canine is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:09:12-07:00","id":1514976,"title":"","content":"I just checked: The descriptive text for the Forms is the same as they used in the <a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/werewolf-the-apocalypse-auspices-and-forms\" target=\"_blank\">dev-blog-post</a> from last October.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:50:25-07:00","id":1514984,"title":"","content":"Wait, that excerpt says that being in a frenzy causes you to <i>lose the wolf</i>. WTF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T10:59:48-07:00","id":1514985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514984#post1514984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, that excerpt says that being in a frenzy causes you to <i>lose the wolf</i>. WTF?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the side-effect of having Rage 0. And &quot;losing the wolf&quot;, I assume, might mean something like you can't shapeshift maybe...?<br /> <br /> So far, it feels to me that the Rage-rating you want to have is 1. That's the optimal middle-point between &quot;losing the wolf&quot; and having to deal with the Messy Criticals and Bestial Failures caused by Rage-Dice.<br /> <br /> Oh, and from the systems we've seen thus far high WP seems like a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T11:50:37-07:00","id":1514989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview#post1514964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Instead of me listing any thoughts, I just have this to say: <b>The char-sheet we saw last week was not only from a playtest but from a previous build of the game!</b> <b>The char-sheet actually doesn't reflect what the final game is like... </b><br /> <br /> Why...?!</div> </div> </div> </div>... perhaps because it's a quick reference, and there wasn't room to put there every detail <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:00:48-07:00","id":1514990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514989#post1514989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... perhaps because it's a quick reference, and there wasn't room to put there every detail<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think putting one asterisk beside &quot;Social and Stealth-Tests: Fail&quot; in order to indicate that (same as with Glabro) specifically non-Intimidation social rolls are talked about there would've been fairly easy if you ask me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:07:58-07:00","id":1514996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514972#post1514972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Hispo<br /> &gt;Dire Wolf<br /> <br /> I realize that this is perhaps the least of the game's sins, but it still makes me want to [SCREAMS EXTERNALLY].<br /> <br /> Dire wolves were about as related to timber wolves as dholes or African painted dogs, which is to say, not particularly closely. They were also not nearly as large as the giant depictions that have been spawned by that one chart transposition from the AD&amp;D 2e Monstrous Compendium, which switched their size with that of worgs (check the 1e MM; dire wolves are Size M). Here, I'd hope this wouldn't be repeated again.<br /> <br /> (Also, they were unique to the Americas, and primarily North America. Not anywhere else. You find a lot of their remains in the LaBrea tar pits, actually.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the debate over the precise lineage of the dire wolf has been very much in the air until quite recent times - damn, it was still mostly heated debate and conjecture at the time of <b>W20</b> came out, afaik.<br /> <br /> But your frustration over correlating their dimensions to the Hispo, yeah, that's ludricous outside of anything beside artistic license on level with 007's license to kill. <br /> <br /> Considering the sheer difference in stats, i always imagined the Hispo (that is <i><b>much</b></i> closer to the Crinos than Lupus) more like the creature in American Werewolf in London or a Worg than anything resembling wolves, dire wolves or any related canines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T12:34:15-07:00","id":1514999,"title":"","content":"So, WW and WtA never been great references to biology and corelated areas (like paleontology, systematics, taxonomy, etc.). Remember, Mokol\u00e9 can be crocodiles, aligators, jacar\u00e9, and... lizards. Which is kind of weird since Crocodilia is most closely related to birds. I try not to bring real biology knowledge when I read the books (I can change that in my table after). Also, the 'dire wol' can only be a nickname for Hispo? Like, as if to say, &quot;This form is like a wolf, but dire&quot; and not the actual fossil species...<br /> <br /> But regard the frenzy rules... yeah, need kill things while in Crinos to avoid must spend WP or enter in frenzy is better solution... I thing no problems here, but the generic dice bonus to the forms still strange...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T13:42:57-07:00","id":1515009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514984#post1514984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, that excerpt says that being in a frenzy causes you to <i>lose the wolf</i>. WTF?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Beast Primal there's a satiety meter that if the monster is fully satisfied it kind of hibernates and you can't use your skills until it's hungry again, I assume the same concept applies here, if the &quot;inner wolf&quot; rage run out, it's rest, I think this term is valid and until the rage is induced again it can't be used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:06:19-07:00","id":1515015,"title":"","content":"Another thing I've noticed: You definitely want to take only one Touchstone at most and be sure said Touchstone is safe at all times. Because these are two rules we've seen in the previews thus far:<ul><li>When a Touchstone is threatened or injured as a result of the Garou\u2019s actions (or inaction), the Garou faces a risk of harano (see p. 140)\u200b.</li> <li>The Storyteller can also call for a frenzy test in cases of extreme provocation, such as any harming of Touchstones, in which case a Willpower test must be made against a Difficulty of 2 (or 3 in crinos form).\u200b</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:08:27-07:00","id":1515016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514996#post1514996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering the sheer difference in stats, i always imagined the Hispo (that is <i><b>much</b></i> closer to the Crinos than Lupus) more like the creature in American Werewolf in London or a Worg than anything resembling wolves, dire wolves or any related canines.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was also how it was consistently portrayed in the older editions. In W20, hispo is twice as tall at the shoulder than lupus, and weighs about five times as much. The large end of hispo used to get into the lower range of a standard horse.<br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;dire wolves&quot; because of RPG compounding of badly used words from older texts is certainly annoying, but the idea is &quot;monster wolf,&quot; not, &quot;turn into the extinct real world animal called the dire wolf.&quot; Though W5 has reduced the &quot;monster wolf&quot; a lot; at least visually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514999#post1514999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but the generic dice bonus to the forms still strange...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering that, for the most part, there isn't a functional difference in the WoD5 rules between temporarily increasing your Strength by 2, or getting +2 dice on Strength rolls. There's just less places where you compared your rating itself to some metric instead of rolling the dice (or assuming the results of rolling the dice via take half). There's no lifting chart where +4 dice to Strength rolls doesn't actually help you lift things,but +4 Strength would increase your lifting massively.<br /> <br /> WoD5 (presumably they're not changing this for W5) also copies the CofD and has Health and Willpower based on your Attributes. If you took a flat -2 to all your social Attributes instead of social dice pools, you'd lose 2 WP a well.<br /> <br /> So there's some decent design reasons for moving to dice bonuses here instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T14:20:21-07:00","id":1515018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515009#post1515009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Beast Primal there's a satiety meter that if the monster is fully satisfied it kind of hibernates and you can't use your skills until it's hungry again, I assume the same concept applies here, if the &quot;inner wolf&quot; rage run out, it's rest, I think this term is valid and until the rage is induced again it can't be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if the situation was similar to Vampire where the Beast was something added onto the character later in life, it would make sense. But garou are born and so there is no external beast, just their core nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T15:42:31-07:00","id":1515026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515018#post1515018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if the situation was similar to Vampire where the Beast was something added onto the character later in life, it would make sense. But garou are born and so there is no external beast, just their core nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was just a comparison to make sense of the phrase, like, I think the intention is to make the rage a game of balance, after they are already changing a lot of things, would it be strange for them to change this detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T16:12:59-07:00","id":1515030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515016#post1515016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was also how it was consistently portrayed in the older editions. In W20, hispo is twice as tall at the shoulder than lupus, and weighs about five times as much. The large end of hispo used to get into the lower range of a standard horse.<br /> <br /> Calling them &quot;dire wolves&quot; because of RPG compounding of badly used words from older texts is certainly annoying, but the idea is &quot;monster wolf,&quot; not, &quot;turn into the extinct real world animal called the dire wolf.&quot; Though W5 has reduced the &quot;monster wolf&quot; a lot; at least visually.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And how. On a complete aside, the Gangrel player in my current V20-ish game is giddy happy with my rebalancing of the disciplines - paying vitae on Shape of the Beast to turn into a Hispo-like battle form instead of a &quot;common&quot; wolf makes a world of difference in action. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T16:19:41-07:00","id":1515032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515026#post1515026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was just a comparison to make sense of the phrase, like, I think the intention is to make the rage a game of balance, after they are already changing a lot of things, would it be strange for them to change this detail?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the balance was Rage vs. Gnosis. They could have built on that instead of rehashing Vampire themes, tinkered with how the game approaches it and make it the game. It would probably be less complicated than tracking W5's despair vs urgency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T16:24:52-07:00","id":1515033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1514971#post1514971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then it also mentions how certain Gifts and other abilities can also end your Frenzy... while also saying that you can't use Gifts while in Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I interpreted that to mean that there are Gifts that can be used to end Frenzy on another person. So Player A enters Frenzy, and while she can't use Gifts, Player B has a gift that can be used to end Player A's Frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T16:36:23-07:00","id":1515034,"title":"","content":"An idea I had, if the intention was to limit the Crinos form why not add a control bar (working name) that fills at one point for each turn the PC is in Crinos form, when the bar exceeds its willpower the character goes into frenzy being controlled by the Storyteller, as optional you can add that it is possible to contain this bar using willpower or that rage points spent during the transformation will also make the bar be filled or also that it decreases by one point at the end of each scene. I took this off the cuff, but what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T18:17:13-07:00","id":1515040,"title":"","content":"Crinos form shouldn't be limited like that. What limits it is the danger to the Veil; as such, you should adopt something more like Heat from the past two editions of Shadowrun, rather than an auto-frenzy mechanic. Call it... Exposure, perhaps. At low levels, no one knows that there's anything about, so any investigation complications or visits from other occult beings are cursory. Increase Exposure, and you start attracting game hunters who have heard about bears in the area; then it progresses to something like SAD agents or Pinkertons, then to deniable assets that have some kind of supernatural powers, and then more blatant enemies of The People. At the highest levels, it might even partially compromise the capacity of Crinos to inflict the Delirium, courtesy of pulling everyone through the Veil. Also, the other Garou might disappear you to save everyone else; certainly, you won't be allowed in a caern if someone is hunting for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T19:19:20-07:00","id":1515048,"title":"","content":"So something like the SI? It's not really a bad ideia, you could even introduce a no-wyrm related antagonist like a cult of shapeshifters hunters, a enemy of the same level, it could be good, but my question is, what you do when are no risk for the veil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T20:47:25-07:00","id":1515056,"title":"","content":"I'm uncertain what to think of this. This is certainly a change, but not an unexpected one.<br /> <br /> In older editions, there wasn't any real drawback to going into Crinos, other than possibly breaking the Veil I guess. You could spend most or all of your time in Crinos without any ill effects. I never had an issue with that, but it seems in W5 they don't want that to be the case. In W5 you won't be able to spend more than a handful of turns in Crinos since you'll drain your Willpower so quickly, so entering Crinos will likely be something a player only does once per session, and even then just for a few turns. If there's multiple instances of combat in a W5 session I think players will end up spending most of it in Glabro (if they want to use human weapons) or Hispo (if they want the aggravated bite). <br /> <br /> I don't know if that's necessarily a bad thing or not. In prior editions, Glabro and Hispo were generally useless since you'd just go into Crinos for combat. In this edition they're be much more important, arguably as important as Crinos is.<br /> <br /> Still, overall I feel like the rules for Crinos are a bit too punishing. Without doing any playtesting, and assuming that the &quot;time limit&quot; on Crinos is necessary to begin with, I'd lean towards making a player spend a Willpower point per turn, unless they successfully land an attack during the turn, in which case the willpower point is not needed (not just successfully kill a target) This can extend the time they spend in Crinos, while still limiting its duration. Plus if the player transforms and keeps missing they'll end up burning through willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T22:12:28-07:00","id":1515059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515056#post1515056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm uncertain what to think of this. This is certainly a change, but not an unexpected one.<br /> <br /> In older editions, there wasn't any real drawback to going into Crinos, other than possibly breaking the Veil I guess. You could spend most or all of your time in Crinos without any ill effects. I never had an issue with that, but it seems in W5 they don't want that to be the case. In W5 you won't be able to spend more than a handful of turns in Crinos since you'll drain your Willpower so quickly, so entering Crinos will likely be something a player only does once per session, and even then just for a few turns. If there's multiple instances of combat in a W5 session I think players will end up spending most of it in Glabro (if they want to use human weapons) or Hispo (if they want the aggravated bite).<br /> <br /> I don't know if that's necessarily a bad thing or not. In prior editions, Glabro and Hispo were generally useless since you'd just go into Crinos for combat. In this edition they're be much more important, arguably as important as Crinos is.<br /> <br /> Still, overall I feel like the rules for Crinos are a bit too punishing. Without doing any playtesting, and assuming that the &quot;time limit&quot; on Crinos is necessary to begin with, I'd lean towards making a player spend a Willpower point per turn, unless they successfully land an attack during the turn, in which case the willpower point is not needed (not just successfully kill a target) This can extend the time they spend in Crinos, while still limiting its duration. Plus if the player transforms and keeps missing they'll end up burning through willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that a Crinos having some limitation would be a good idea, but using willpower? Are you sure this is a good idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T22:51:02-07:00","id":1515061,"title":"","content":"Willpower will dissapear very quickly from sheet if player would turn to crinos. I don't like it, cause it seems that shifting into it is the last option on the list. I don't like either turning crinos into savage mindless killing machine that can't use gifts. It's too gauru for me, and gauru in Forsaken was something that I couldn't get along with. I like glabro in W5, it's quite good designed. <br /> Suprisingly still crinos with those boosts will tear almost through everything.<br /> Now I am curious about existence of Spirit of the Fray - if it's permanent, or some other gifts are maby crinos gift exclusion have some sense. <br /> Second thing I'm curious about is silver in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T23:48:03-07:00","id":1515070,"title":"","content":"Another way I could see the Crinos-Form and Frenzy being used is as a way to purge your Rage-track. Let's say you got a character who due to Rage-Checks and story-events has Rage 4 or 5. One super-quick way to deal with that is to look for enemies, shift into Crinos and then <i>voluntarily </i>enter Frenzy. That way you don't need to pay the WP but only have to pass a WP-test to make sure you <i>only </i>kill every enemy in sight. And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> you're probably right about the Gifts being mentioned coming from other Garou and so this would be a way to safely get someone out of Frenzy, I imagine, without relying on a WP-test. And after that your Rage drops to 0.<br /> <br /> What's missing for me here is how the Hauglosk-tracker figures into this. I would assume any dealings with Frenzy or high Rage would call for checks on that tracker but there's nothing here. I guess we'll see how that exactly works...<br /> <br /> Another thing is it does feel like you'd wanna avoid raising your Rage which means anything calling for Rage/Frenzy-checks (shifting into anything besides Homid or Lupus, Gifts, Rites, your Touchstone being anywhere near danger...) are stuff you learn to avoid. And that means less Gifts, Rites and shifting will happen during the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T01:41:55-07:00","id":1515073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515059#post1515059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that a Crinos having some limitation would be a good idea, but using willpower? Are you sure this is a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know? I haven't seen the full combat system yet so I don't really answer that. I'm basically just giving the designers the benefit of the doubt. They seem to believe that a temporary Crinos form with a duration largely determined by Willpower is necessary for the purposes of game balance and design. Maybe it's bullshit, but maybe when we see the full rules it'll be more reasonable. Maybe Werewolves have lots of ways to regain Willpower so it's not as big of a stumbling block as it appears in a vacuum? I don't know. <br /> <br /> I'm just thinking that ifit does prove problematic there might be some minor tweaks to allow players to stay in Crinos by adding more conditions to the Willpower-free turns. Right now it's kill something or spend Willpower, but it might be easy to add extra conditions like &quot;successfully deal damage to a target, kill something, or spend Willpower&quot; or &quot;take damage&quot; or something similar. It could be a way to largely stay within the rules-as-writteb while making shifting into Crinos a more attractive option for players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T02:16:56-07:00","id":1515075,"title":"","content":"The drawbacks, complications and considerations of Crinos in W20 were sufficient:<ul><li>-1 difficulty to Rage checks is a double-edged sword; it can protect you, but it can also drive you into Frenzy</li> <li>Against Garou and Fera, it's typically an escalation to warfare, certain death; it declares that you intend to kill them</li> <li>Its size, especially its height and weight, can prove a drawback in some environments</li> <li>Delirium is a double-edged sword; making humans panic and flee can preserve the Veil, but it can also cause chaos or deaths, or cause people you're protecting to run into danger</li> <li>There will be fights where you need to multitask; if you need to speak normally while fighting, Glabro is better, if you need to mobilize very swiftly or hunt something down while fighting, Hispo is better</li> <li>A Crinos form Garou is more likely to encourage other supernaturals to pull out their biggest weapons: Vulgar Magick, Unleashings and so on, meanwhile human-like enemies are more likely to pull out explosives, silver, and weapons which are generally considered overkill</li> </ul>To my taste, if players are only ever using Crinos in a game, or only ever using Crinos+Hispo, it suggests a lot of samey encounters without complications and secondary objectives. In fact the fight should almost always be the secondary objective; if an encounter lacks a primary objective (protect the cubs, stop the fire, secure the data) it could probably use rethinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T02:50:36-07:00","id":1515078,"title":"","content":"The design space for frenzy is an additional reason why the metis wouldn't work in w5. For me the whole thing is rather messy as it completley invalidates the visual identity of Werewolf. Sure, it's a reboot, but it's a reboot where most previous depictions of what crinos looks like in practice and how much it is used can be just tossed in the bin. Crinos used to be a statement, but also a natural part of who you were and a form you are comfortable (if angrier) in. The art and fiction supported this and showed Garou and fera engaging in all kind of activities in their hybrid forms.<br /> <br /> Additional imagery I have issue with is with the tactical approach and the fact that Garou are supposed to be highly organised soldiers. Hispo and Crinos used to be the main fight forms and allowed them the Garou to do complex manouvrers and organise themselves in battle. Lupus was investigation and low profile, homid was low profile. Glabro was get out of trouble without getting too much attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:07:19-07:00","id":1515081,"title":"","content":"Hopefully, they carved out a section in the Storytelling-chapter on what exactly counts as an &quot;extreme provocation&quot;. Because with a bad ST this certainly could become an issue. And you really gotta invest in Composure and Resolve during character-creation. Because one such failed Frenzy-check can really derail whatever situation you're in and then can snowball in addition when you fail the WP-test to stop killing after all your enemies (or source of provocation) are dead.<br /> <br /> Setting-wise this new approach is yet another example of a question I have already wondered about a couple of times during these previews: Sure, the Garou-Nation has fallen - but the way it's set up now my bigger question is how there ever was a Garou-Nation in the first place...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:08:23-07:00","id":1515082,"title":"","content":"One thing I actually don't like about W20, and feel contradicts the artwork and overall vibe of the book, is a passage saying that &quot;even Metis bristle with murderous Rage when in their Crinos form&quot; - it feels contradictory to artwork like the Silent Strider, and the Silver Fang. Let Metis, and indeed open-minded Homid and Lupus, lounge around in their Crinos form. It can be a form for rituals, for recreation, for relaxation, for travel, so long as there aren't any humans nearby. In fact to my taste the biggest impediment to Metis lounging around in their Breed forms, enjoying the body they were born in, should be fundamentalists and bigots within a Sept. You know, the kinds of social tensions you could make some kind of modern/urban supernatural horror setting around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:09:41-07:00","id":1515083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515081#post1515081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully, they carved out a section in the Storytelling-chapter on what exactly counts as an &quot;extreme provocation&quot;. Because with a bad ST this certainly could become an issue. And you really gotta invest in Composure and Resolve during character-creation. Because one such failed Frenzy-check can really derail whatever situation you're in and then can snowball in addition when you fail the WP-test to stop killing after all your enemies (or source of provocation) are dead.<br /> <br /> Setting-wise this new approach is yet another example of a question I have already wondered about a couple of times during these previews: Sure, the Garou-Nation has fallen - but the way it's set up now my bigger question is how there ever was a Garou-Nation in the first place...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that way about the compulsion-y stuff in V5 - with Vampires messing things up so badly, so frequently, and becoming hungry and stereotyped and unhinged every time they try something difficult, how the hell is there a Masquerade, or a Camarilla, or any Sect at all in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:37:05-07:00","id":1515087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515081#post1515081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Setting-wise this new approach is yet another example of a question I have already wondered about a couple of times during these previews: Sure, the Garou-Nation has fallen - but the way it's set up now my bigger question is how there ever was a Garou-Nation in the first place...?</div> </div> </div> </div>No joke, I constantly get the feeling that the Garou Nation is literally the Nation from 1-20 eds from the way it is worded and presented. That the Elders are 20th ed. garou and the W5 pcs are the Hot New Thing garou.<br /> <br /> Because the alternative makes no sense, given how the tribes are described alone.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:48:22-07:00","id":1515089,"title":"","content":"Another thing about the setting... Now that we've learned a bit more about Rage and Frenzy, I also gotta wonder: If that's what the situation is like for PC-Garou - how exactly can the Get of Fenris function as a Tribe, let alone as Packs...? If normal Garou have to test for Frenzy when there's an &quot;extreme provocation&quot;, I assume the Get's Frenzy is on a hair-trigger-release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T03:50:18-07:00","id":1515090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515087#post1515087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No joke, I constantly get the feeling that the Garou Nation is literally the Nation from 1-20 eds from the way it is worded and presented. That the Elders are 20th ed. garou and the W5 pcs are the Hot New Thing garou.<br /> <br /> Because the alternative makes no sense, given how the tribes are described alone.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In that case they're in for a rude awakening if they ever get into a fight with any of the Elders...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:07:15-07:00","id":1515092,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder about one thing; Given the insistence that hispo and lupus could be mistaken for big dogs, could we actually end up having dog shifters running around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:30:45-07:00","id":1515095,"title":"","content":"I really dislike that by the way.<br /> <br /> No one with any sense or familiarity with canids mistakes a wolf for a dog. Wolves are typically significantly bigger than dogs, and they have a different shape. There is a type of dog which can be mistaken for a wolf, and visa versa, but that's an edge case. But even then I understand going &quot;Lupus can be mistaken for a big dog&quot; - because people WOULD mistake it for a big dog, especially in areas where there aren't any wolves.<br /> <br /> Hispo is huge compared to a wolf. And wolves are huge. Hispo is an enormous primordial predator which stalked the edges of the first cities. They aren't &quot;big dog sized&quot;, they're absolutely enormous.<br /> <br /> It feels like making all the forms smaller (the Crinos looks pitifully small, and not particularly muscular either) is perhaps part of a trend of antipathy towards the very idea of the Werewolf. My hot take is that people writing an edition of WTA should be stoked about Werewolves and really really love them. As it stands the &quot;Werewolf&quot; part feels like an afterthought, with mechanics existing to punish you for ever daring to take the form where people will ever go &quot;yep, that's a giant wolf monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> It feels like the Werewolf has been figuratively neutered/spayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:48:33-07:00","id":1515098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515095#post1515095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike that by the way.<br /> <br /> No one with any sense or familiarity with canids mistakes a wolf for a dog. Wolves are typically significantly bigger than dogs, and they have a different shape. There is a type of dog which can be mistaken for a wolf, and visa versa, but that's an edge case. But even then I understand going &quot;Lupus can be mistaken for a big dog&quot; - because people WOULD mistake it for a big dog, especially in areas where there aren't any wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say it is the opposite, some people are VERY gun-ho about taking out wolves and many huskies have gotten shot due to it. So I would say the lupus would be very much getting shot at/have animal control getting called on them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:52:06-07:00","id":1515099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515098#post1515098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd actually say it is the opposite, some people are VERY gun-ho about taking out wolves and many huskies have gotten shot due to it. So I would say the lupus would be very much getting shot at/have animal control getting called on them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that will be happening in areas where people know wolves are around, and are thus scared of anything that looks like a wolf right?<br /> <br /> For instance if a Lupus Garou is lying down next to an oven inside a cottage, or playing with toddlers in a garden, any sane onlooker would go &quot;wow, that big dog looks a lot like a wolf!&quot; not &quot;wow that wolf is behaving in a very dog-like manner!&quot;. I get what you're saying, and I agree, but my baseline is assuming that if a Garou wants to be mistaken for a dog, they will go to places wolves won't go, and behave in ways wolves don't, at which point it's easier to assume they're a big sharp dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:19:35-07:00","id":1515107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515098#post1515098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd actually say it is the opposite, some people are VERY gun-ho about taking out wolves and many huskies have gotten shot due to it. So I would say the lupus would be very much getting shot at/have animal control getting called on them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly anyone who mistakes a husky for a wolf should immediately have their firearms seized and their drivers license revoked because they do not have the eyesight or brainpower to operate either a firearm or a vehicle.<br /> <br /> An average wolf weighs more than twice what an average husky weighs and is almost twice the height at the withers.......then again we've all heard of hunters who shot their kid or friend because they thought they were a deer or badger.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-15-2023, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:27:42-07:00","id":1515110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515095#post1515095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike that by the way.<br /> <br /> No one with any sense or familiarity with canids mistakes a wolf for a dog. Wolves are typically significantly bigger than dogs, and they have a different shape. There is a type of dog which can be mistaken for a wolf, and visa versa, but that's an edge case. But even then I understand going &quot;Lupus can be mistaken for a big dog&quot; - because people WOULD mistake it for a big dog, especially in areas where there aren't any wolves.<br /> <br /> Hispo is huge compared to a wolf. And wolves are huge. Hispo is an enormous primordial predator which stalked the edges of the first cities. They aren't &quot;big dog sized&quot;, they're absolutely enormous.<br /> <br /> It feels like making all the forms smaller (the Crinos looks pitifully small, and not particularly muscular either) is perhaps part of a trend of antipathy towards the very idea of the Werewolf. My hot take is that people writing an edition of WTA should be stoked about Werewolves and really really love them. As it stands the &quot;Werewolf&quot; part feels like an afterthought, with mechanics existing to punish you for ever daring to take the form where people will ever go &quot;yep, that's a giant wolf monster&quot;.<br /> <br /> It feels like the Werewolf has been figuratively neutered/spayed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The direct quotes from the Developer and Community manager and the excerpts have described Lupus form as ' like a GSD'......which is just utterly bullshit unless your looking at the Golden Wolf ( formerly Golden Jackal) and even they tend to be longer and taller than a GSD.<br /> <br /> Hispo is described as ' a big dog'.....the biggest remotely &quot;wolf shaped&quot; dog would be a Malamute which at 45kg is tiny compared to average wolf weights........perhaps they mean something like an Irish Wolf Hound which is longer and taller than a wolf but much lighter......and also could not be mistaken for a wolf by anyone with a brain.<br /> <br /> Its baffling.<br /> <br /> Its definitely the Werewolf game you'd make if you didn't want to make a Werewolf game......which kinda tracks based on what we know of the development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:34:46-07:00","id":1515111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515107#post1515107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly anyone who mistakes a husky for a wolf should immediately have their firearms seized and their drivers license revoked because they do not have the eyesight or brainpower to operate either a firearm or a vehicle.<br /> <br /> An average wolf weighs more than twice what an average husky weighs and is almost twice the height at the withers.......then again we've all heard of hunters who shot their kid or friend because they thought they were a deer or badger.....</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to link the stories because they are heartbreaking, but it does happen enough that I could see it in WoD.<br /> <br /> I just mean that 'that's a big dog' would not be the kind of defence a garou in lupus wants.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T07:29:49-07:00","id":1515122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515092#post1515092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder about one thing; Given the insistence that hispo and lupus could be mistaken for big dogs, could we actually end up having dog shifters running around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things about this: If the developers actually bought into the notion of the Lupus Form just looking like a &quot;big dog&quot; and the Hispo Form merely being a &quot;really big dog&quot; then, on one hand, why not give the Lupus Form a flat two-dice bonus to Stealth rolls (since they are so innocuous-looking according to this description) and on the other hand where is the Stealth-penalty for the Hispo coming from then (it's just the innocuous-looking Lupus form but a bit bigger after all)? The second thing... looking at the art, doesn't it feel like the artist actually followed the &quot;big dog&quot;/&quot;really big dog&quot;-descriptions there...? Because the Hispo-form really does look like a merely slightly bigger wolf there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T09:06:22-07:00","id":1515136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515111#post1515111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want to link the stories because they are heartbreaking, but it does happen enough that I could see it in WoD.<br /> <br /> I just mean that 'that's a big dog' would not be the kind of defence a garou in lupus wants.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I've seen the stories. And despite their statements I believe every single one of those people adsolutely knew they were shooting a family pet and not a wolf ( not that any of the ones I read had received a federal permit necessary to hunt wolves anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T09:10:15-07:00","id":1515137,"title":"","content":"I'm about to just start bashing my head against a wall.<br /> <br /> Apparently the Crinos mechanics aren't an issue because they last for a scene and the ST can just say the scene is over so theres no need to worry about Frenzy........I mean this is the same redditor that stated a Scene in H5 could essentially be an entire day......but sure. All Mechanics issues are now to be solved by ST fiat so we are no longer allowed to query them......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T10:01:13-07:00","id":1515145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515061#post1515061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower will dissapear very quickly from sheet if player would turn to crinos. I don't like it, cause it seems that shifting into it is the last option on the list. I don't like either turning crinos into savage mindless killing machine that can't use gifts. It's too gauru for me, and gauru in Forsaken was something that I couldn't get along with. I like glabro in W5, it's quite good designed.<br /> Suprisingly still crinos with those boosts will tear almost through everything.<br /> Now I am curious about existence of Spirit of the Fray - if it's permanent, or some other gifts are maby crinos gift exclusion have some sense.<br /> Second thing I'm curious about is silver in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no contact with the gauru, are they too different of the Garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T10:05:55-07:00","id":1515146,"title":"","content":"So is their an explanation as to why they're decentivising the crinos form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T10:10:17-07:00","id":1515148,"title":"","content":"I have the nasty feeling because whoever designed (or the whole W5 for that matter) it either hate Werewolf: the Apocalypse or completly out of touch of the game and/or playerbase...<br /> ...or both <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Honestly, neither is a good thing<br /> Really I have a &quot;Disney bought Star Wars and making films&quot; PTSD all over again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T10:20:04-07:00","id":1515149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515148#post1515148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the nasty feeling because whoever designed (or the whole W5 for that matter) it either hate Werewolf: the Apocalypse or completly out of touch of the game and/or playerbase...<br /> ...or both <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Honestly, neither is a good thing<br /> Really I have a &quot;Disney bought Star Wars and making films&quot; PTSD all over again...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just a teenwolf fan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T10:30:56-07:00","id":1515150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515146#post1515146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is their an explanation as to why they're decentivising the crinos form?</div> </div> </div> </div>One comment you got multiple times last October in Outstar-interview and the Discord Q&amp;A was about this sentiment (and this is from the latter):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you share anything about how Rage mechanics will work at this stage?<br /> Still in active development. Everything touches it or vice versa, so it's a lot of work. The general target is &quot;<b>great for when you want a violent outcome, awful for when you want any other outcome.</b>&quot; </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> This and the line from this latest preview:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This can be <b>voluntarily</b>, as a response to overwhelming odds, or involuntarily if the Garou\u2019s Willpower is completely depleted.\u200b </div> </div> </div>\u200b(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> I thought about both of these things when I realized that the &quot;Kill something or pay 1 WP per turn - or Frenzy.&quot; isn't the only approach here. If you're fine with a violent outcome, you're actually <i>supposed to</i> shift into Crinos and <i>voluntarily</i> trigger Frenzy, I think.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, from the Discord Q&amp;A:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will Rage still be a barrier for basic contact between mortals and Garou?<br /> Not a mechanically-enforced hard system. More a question of risks, because of the <b>volatility </b>of the Garou. </div> </div> </div>(Emphasis mine)<br /> <br /> Volatility... That's another word that came up quite a few times last October when Garou were described. Who knows how this all works in the context of the Harano/Hauglosk-tracks but with the Frenzy-system we already got this tidbit that whatever the ST deems an &quot;extreme provocation&quot; for the Garou allows them to call for a Frenzy/WP-test. And so I think this word &quot;volatility&quot; does seem like a central concept for what the developers thought Garou are like.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thematical direction of all of this is &quot;Being a werewolf sucks...&quot; and you gotta wonder how this is supposed to fit into a setting where you supposedly still care about fighting the Wyrm and making things better. And even though the setting is mid-Apocalypse the previews so far are still talking about &quot;fighting back&quot; or sentiments of that sort. So the writing didn't really follow up or double down on the premise, it feels like.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T10:47:02-07:00","id":1515152,"title":"","content":"This is probably against the spirit of the rules but technically follows them. If crinos grants a bonus to all physical rolls such as lockpicking, but you need to check for frenzy every round you don't kill something there is a simple, yet stupid solution. Take a bag of pet store crickets with you to pick a lock in crinos and take a break each round to quickly squish one.<br /> <br /> You technically meet the requirements of killing something each round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T