ts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:14:27-07:00","id":1515247,"title":"","content":"Something brought up in a reddit thread about these previews; To some the limits in crinos reflect the traditional werewolf more. Which would be great.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that was the reason it was limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:26:25-07:00","id":1515248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515247#post1515247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something brought up in a reddit thread about these previews; To some the limits in crinos reflect the traditional werewolf more. Which would be great.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that was the reason it was limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what could be the reason?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:43:05-07:00","id":1515249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515248#post1515248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what could be the reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>A few come to mind. Firstly, there's the carryover effect of porting over Forsaken. Secondly, there's probably some variety of directive to flatten out power curves for crossover reasons. Thirdly, people keep ranting about Crinos and miniature golf and other such intentionally absurd juxtapositions chosen to make any length of time in Crinos beyond a few seconds seem ridiculous.<br /> <br /> None of it is expressly needed. Werewolf is not supposed to be Vampire, and it does poorly when forced to be Vampire. Once more, insert your favorite joke about Abominations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T08:44:47-07:00","id":1515250,"title":"","content":"So ignoring any legacy-stuff and thinking purely of W5 and what this game is aiming for... I think for me a lot depends on the Harano/Hauglosk-tracker. This is pure speculation but something I could imagine from what we know so far and is something I certainly wouldn't like is that this game really focuses on werewolves having a fragile/unstable psyche. Like, theoretically what if it's set up like this: Severe provocation - Frenzy check; Big setback/Traumatic event/Serious injury - Harano check; Bad guys escaped/Innocents get harmed/Bad guys advanced their agenda - Hauglosk check. So the game focuses on the werewolves' continually deteriorating psyche that is always at risk of breaking (which then results either in Frenzy, Harano or Hauglosk). And in the same way vampires can never escape their bloodthirst, the werewolves can never escape their volatile psyche that snaps into these extreme sets of behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T10:43:56-07:00","id":1515264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515249#post1515249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A few come to mind. Firstly, there's the carryover effect of porting over Forsaken. Secondly, there's probably some variety of directive to flatten out power curves for crossover reasons. Thirdly, people keep ranting about Crinos and miniature golf and other such intentionally absurd juxtapositions chosen to make any length of time in Crinos beyond a few seconds seem ridiculous.<br /> <br /> None of it is expressly needed. Werewolf is not supposed to be Vampire, and it does poorly when forced to be Vampire. Once more, insert your favorite joke about Abominations.</div> </div> </div> </div>On twitter everyone looks like an abomination embraced by a Brujah with explosive temper syndrome and I couldn't resist sending this one. Anyway I've been looking at the WtF story and asked about the VtR backstory, and strangely it seems like they want to put the themes from there over here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:14:27-07:00","id":1515268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515247#post1515247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something brought up in a reddit thread about these previews; To some the limits in crinos reflect the traditional werewolf more. Which would be great.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that was the reason it was limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>The traditional well wolf lore is a bunch of folk stores about how you're an evil witch or zues is pissed of at you. The fuck are they talking talking about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:43:45-07:00","id":1515274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515268#post1515268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The traditional well wolf lore is a bunch of folk stores about how you're an evil witch or zues is pissed of at you. The fuck are they talking talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>They think the &quot;traditional werewolf&quot; was born of horror movies, I assume. I don't think most people are aware that folklore exists (or don't recognise stuff like Lykaon as being relevant to the pop-culture werewolf they imagine when you say the word)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-16-2023, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T11:55:59-07:00","id":1515276,"title":"","content":"In central Europe before X century belived and told tales about slavic tribe wandering through lands by night as wolves, so shapeshifting legends have a long history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:04:44-07:00","id":1515280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515274#post1515274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They think the &quot;traditional werewolf&quot; was born of horror movies, I assume. I don't think most people are aware that folklore exists (or don't recognise stuff like Lykaon as being relevant to the pop-culture werewolf they imagine when you say the word)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the werewolf they want is the American Werewolf in X, the Bad Moon werewolf, and the Wolf-Man werewolf. A monstrous creature that loses control of itself and tears apart things with ease.,<br /> <br /> Actual werewolf folklore and myths are much more nuanced and I might as well link one of my favourite sources here: <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/177987070427/werewolves\" target=\"_blank\">https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com...427/werewolves</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:50:35-07:00","id":1515286,"title":"","content":"The problem is that even the &quot;sees the moon, transforms, and goes on a murder spree,&quot; pop culture depiction of werewolves doesn't fit W5 Crinos having a time-bomb on it. You'd model that with something like a nearly impossible to resist (at least for starting characters because it would get old, fast) Frenzy check at seeing the full moon (or Auspice moon, or whatever). All of those depictions are based on involuntary shifting as a key part of the narrative.<br /> <br /> Crinos time-bombs for voluntary shifting isn't going to get you American Werewolf in London because that's not how that movie worked.<br /> <br /> Those pop-culture representations also generally show werewolves as more &quot;logical&quot; predators that Hulk-smash machines. They stalk, single out prey, and pounce. They avoid large groups of humans that could try to fight back. They might still be animalistic and driven to violence, but there's some intelligence in going about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:54:21-07:00","id":1515289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515280#post1515280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, the werewolf they want is the American Werewolf in X, the Bad Moon werewolf, and the Wolf-Man werewolf. A monstrous creature that loses control of itself and tears apart things with ease.,<br /> <br /> Actual werewolf folklore and myths are much more nuanced and I might as well link one of my favourite sources here: <a href=\"https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com/post/177987070427/werewolves\" target=\"_blank\">https://maverick-werewolf.tumblr.com...427/werewolves</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's the thing<br /> <br /> 1) they're nothing like wta werewolves thematically<br /> <br /> 2) several of the movie werewolves are cold calculating predators.....like you know, wolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also interested in how they percieve fury and violence in humans and instinct in wolves. Your higher reasoning doesn't genrally check out and wolves I'm not convinced wolves are mindless berserkers when in kill mode.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-16-2023, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:58:42-07:00","id":1515290,"title":"","content":"WtA's Werewolves are more along the lines of mystics bearing animal skins to change into animals, animals changing out of people because of X, but most of all the story of Thiess of Livonia. You know, the one about people changing into werewolves at night to go to hell to fight witches and demons serving Satan. It spawned a whole power metal band <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T13:03:14-07:00","id":1515292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515289#post1515289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the thing<br /> <br /> 1) they're nothing like wta werewolves thematically<br /> <br /> 2) several of the movie werewolves are cold calculating predators.....like you know, wolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also interested in how they percieve fury and violence in humans and instinct in wolves. Your higher reasoning doesn't genrally check out and wolves I'm not convinced wolves are mindless berserkers when in kill mode.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) And that is, as I've stated, something some people want.<br /> <br /> 2) Yep, the 'movie werewolf' is a misnomer, because there is no one true type of one XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T13:13:58-07:00","id":1515293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515290#post1515290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtA's Werewolves are more along the lines of mystics bearing animal skins to change into animals, animals changing out of people because of X, but most of all the story of Thiess of Livonia. You know, the one about people changing into werewolves at night to go to hell to fight witches and demons serving Satan. It spawned a whole power metal band <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the emerging shortcomings of w5 is it isn't very metal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T13:19:40-07:00","id":1515296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515293#post1515293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the emerging shortcomings of w5 is it isn't very metal.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"500\" height=\"275\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://memesbams.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/13-Sad-doctor-who-gif.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://memesbams.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/13-Sad-doctor-who-gif.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://memesbams.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/01/13-Sad-doctor-who-gif.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> Profound... sadness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T16:19:26-07:00","id":1515314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515247#post1515247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something brought up in a reddit thread about these previews; To some the limits in crinos reflect the traditional werewolf more. Which would be great.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that was the reason it was limited.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I still don't get with that logic is that even if you want that out of a werewolf-game and are happy W5 is going down that route... how are you gonna square that with the whole animism/war against the Wyrm-side of things? If players are supposed to really care about this inner struggle with Rage then how will that compare with the other idea of Garou being Gaia's warriors trying to make the world a better place...? From some of these people who say that on Reddit I get the sense they really don't like WtA and are happy with any deviation from the old stuff... but even with all the changes and throwing out old lore, it's not like W5 is a <i>completely new</i> game completely unrelated to its previous editions. So anyone who hates the previous editions of WtA to such a huge degree won't get everything they wished for out of W5 (because on some level there's still parts of WtA in there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T18:18:57-07:00","id":1515321,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder at this point what the current Dev's wider vision for WoD is. So far it's been a massively divisive shift in direction and the angry voices get louder with each release.<br /> <br /> At what point to they look around, see how media doing similar things turned out(*Cough*Starwars*Cough-Cough*) and think &quot;Hey, maybe I don't want to end up like that&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T18:56:18-07:00","id":1515322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515314#post1515314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I still don't get with that logic is that even if you want that out of a werewolf-game and are happy W5 is going down that route... how are you gonna square that with the whole animism/war against the Wyrm-side of things? If players are supposed to really care about this inner struggle with Rage then how will that compare with the other idea of Garou being Gaia's warriors trying to make the world a better place...? From some of these people who say that on Reddit I get the sense they really don't like WtA and are happy with any deviation from the old stuff... but even with all the changes and throwing out old lore, it's not like W5 is a <i>completely new</i> game completely unrelated to its previous editions. So anyone who hates the previous editions of WtA to such a huge degree won't get everything they wished for out of W5 (because on some level there's still parts of WtA in there).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why they hate WtA exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T21:44:20-07:00","id":1515328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515321#post1515321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder at this point what the current Dev's wider vision for WoD is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem is that there isn't a current lead dev. That one that worked on H5 and W5 (and has stated started work on more) left because he had a better job lined up and timed for when development on W5 was supposed to be finished. There's basically just a committee at Paradox working off old developer notes, and whatever freedom they give Renegade (and maybe Onyx Path if Onyx Path makes more WoD5 books at some point, which you'd think Paradox would want because the ones Onyx Path has worked on are considered some top tier books for the line). There is no vision, because there's no experienced TTRPG developer at the top of the decision ladder anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At what point to they look around, see how media doing similar things turned out(*Cough*Starwars*Cough-Cough*) and think &quot;Hey, maybe I don't want to end up like that&quot;. </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure most people would be plenty happy to be Disney with Star Wars right now. For all that their first five movies are divisive, even with the bomb that was Solo financially, those movies paid off everything Disney spent to get Star Wars from Lucas. Focusing on shows for the time being has actually put Star Wars in a great place, as they've been much better received, which is bringing in profits and rebuild fan trust/excitement while they take their time deciding how to move forward with any films.<br /> <br /> Sure, you'd rather have had five blockbusters with great reception and great profits than what happened, but a rough start that you're actually recovering from and regardless of Internet reviews you still made a ton of money off of (even if most of that just wrote off the cost of buying the rights in the first place) is a lot better than most TTRPG companies could hope for.<br /> <br /> In the end how we all feel bout W5's RPG books basically isn't going to matter to Paradox. What's going to matter is if they can start making high profit projects in other markets (like, you know, video games from the video game company); Bloodlines 2 can be divisive and never really reach the classic status as the first, but if it sells well, they can actually put a dent in al the red from buying the WW IPs and the long development cycle for BL2, they can make their investors happy, and attract more projects by proving that VtM/WoD is still a brand big enough to really carry a franchise of video games, some streaming shows, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T01:07:15-07:00","id":1515335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515321#post1515321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder at this point what the current Dev's wider vision for WoD is. So far it's been a massively divisive shift in direction and the angry voices get louder with each release.<br /> <br /> At what point to they look around, see how media doing similar things turned out(*Cough*Starwars*Cough-Cough*) and think &quot;Hey, maybe I don't want to end up like that&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Star wars is a big enough franchise to soldier forward through a series of gaffes. W5's position is a lot more precarious. Paradox are probably more focused on it as a franchise to sell games and such.<br /> <br /> I think were going to get to a point were the negative start to impact product value but thats a while off. In the meantime the crunch is how well w5 does, if it does well it doesn't matter that the product has zero respect for the game or consumers. If it undersells or tanks that might give them pause for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T03:15:11-07:00","id":1515339,"title":"","content":"Just trying to itemize some issues.<br /> <br /> -<b>Glabro </b>causes vertical growth but the muscles look leaner because... the writer thinks tall and low body fat is peak fitness? Aesthetics? Hypertrophy is gross but six packs are good? You know a visible six pack is just a sign you don't eat enough, right? Someone has some very specific ideas on what is peak performance and I can't think of a rationale behind it bar ill-informed personal taste. <br /> <br /> -Frenzying because you in <b>Crinos</b> didn't kill someone that turn is just such a riot. Like that's such a GAME mechanic. It doesn't belong in a serious roleplaying environment. <br /> -How do Garou have Klaive duels if they can't control themselves in Grinos? How do Garou learn to fight if they can't control themselves in crinos? Have they considered how the Crinos form being unusable would impact umbral exploration? It's like the best form the majority of the time. <br /> -How do Garou feel about being Gaia's murderers rather than Gaia's warriors? <br /> -Metis<br /> <br /> -If Hispo is a really big dog what the fuck is lupus, a puppy? <br /> -Why can hispo speak and why only edgy words? I reckon if I could say &quot;kill&quot; I could also say 'uh-huh' or something more measured like that. It's like the writer is so invested in making C-list horror villains they forgot players like to think for themselves. <br /> -As many have pointed out, direwolves are a different species, just use magic to give me a pony-sized monster wolf and don't bother with pretensions of being 'smart'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T04:23:10-07:00","id":1515341,"title":"","content":"If they want to make a Werewolf: The Apocalypse game that is <b><i>not</i></b> Werewolf: The Apocalypse, fine, okay, but damn, then don't call it Werewolf: The Apocalypse!<br /> For three decades that name ment something!<br /> ....and <i>not </i><i>this</i> where W5 is going<br /> Hell, I will just call it &quot;5&quot;; like the 1998 Zilla is not worthy the &quot;God&quot; prefix, nor this worthy to the &quot;W&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515339#post1515339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-How do Garou have Klaive duels if they can't control themselves in Grinos?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they even know what Klaviskar<i> is</i>, why is important...<br /> ...and don't even dream abput the Children of Gaia' Iskakku, <i>The Way of the Staff </i>or god forbid, Kailindo, the shapeshifting martial art developed by the Stargazers...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T04:56:06-07:00","id":1515347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515322#post1515322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why they hate WtA exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many reasons; Not the kind of werewolf they want, think the Save the Earth plot is too goofy, don't like that WtA has furry fans,etc.<br /> <br /> And I need to note, all of those things are FINE. Tastes vary.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T05:02:42-07:00","id":1515348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515347#post1515347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WtA has furry fans,etc.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably worth noting the crinos rules are a bit of a buzzkill for them and their plans to play an sexy anthro wolf. Jokes about furries aside, it seems odd to discourage a section of the fanbase/potential fanbase from picking up your book.<br /> <br /> furries throw a lot of cash around and the game wasn't nicknamed &quot;furry captain planet&quot; for nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-17-2023, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T05:43:39-07:00","id":1515354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515339#post1515339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just trying to itemize some issues.<br /> <br /> -<b>Glabro </b>causes vertical growth but the muscles look leaner because... the writer thinks tall and low body fat is peak fitness? Aesthetics? Hypertrophy is gross but six packs are good? You know a visible six pack is just a sign you don't eat enough, right? Someone has some very specific ideas on what is peak performance and I can't think of a rationale behind it bar ill-informed personal taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't any weirder than truly thinking through the implications of something as broad as &quot;physical dice bonus&quot;. For example, it makes Glabro the form to use for Driving, I guess... lol<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515339#post1515339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Frenzying because you in <b>Crinos</b> didn't kill someone that turn is just such a riot. Like that's such a GAME mechanic. It doesn't belong in a serious roleplaying environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of the two ways to enter Frenzy, the one where anything the ST considers an &quot;extreme provocation&quot; leads to a Frenzy check/WP-test is worse. At least with the Crinos Form there is a way to mitigate it somewhat. With an &quot;extreme provocation&quot;, it really is only one dice-roll that separates you from your character being forced into Frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515339#post1515339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-How do Garou have Klaive duels if they can't control themselves in Grinos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple Answer: They don't. In W5 you can't use weapons in the Crinos Form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515339#post1515339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Metis</div> </div> </div> </div>Crinos-born Garou don't exist in W5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T06:25:18-07:00","id":1515355,"title":"","content":"The MO seems to be &quot;Vampire was the most popular, so make everything look like Vampire to maximize monetization&quot;, with a side of a large, scummy corporation not liking that the game loudly shouts that large, scummy corporations are inherently aligned with a malignant spiritual force that twists and sickens the universe. With Vampire, there's some insulation between the text and subtext condemning older orders that have grown corrupt, but Werewolf's text is &quot;this is bad, Rage against it!&quot;. As a result, corporate pushes a &quot;street&quot; focus that's completely unearned and not even remotely authentic, in addition to flattening the play styles out further, in order to distract from the original narrative. The Apocalypse has already happened, there's no reason to do more than just try to survive, certainly not trying to make a difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515354#post1515354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't any weirder than truly thinking through the implications of something as broad as &quot;physical dice bonus&quot;. For example, it makes Glabro the form to use for Driving, I guess... lol</div> </div> </div> </div><i>An American Werewolf in Traffic</i>. &quot;Now that I'm driving, those caribou don't stand a chance!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T06:45:55-07:00","id":1515357,"title":"","content":"Save the earth plot seems more relevant now. It takes a war on for europeans to get somewhat serious about replacing fossil fuels, and even then it's just an economic incentive. .<br /> <br /> Yeah, furries are gross. Any kind of sexual act that isn't for the purpose of procreation should really earn you the death penalty in my humble eyes, but the WoD gameline has always been more a toolbox than a story (metaplot be damned) . Most characters in rollplaying games can do everything a human can and more, so unless the game specifically rules it out there's no mechanism to stop your character from committing acts of heinous sadism, beyond the actions of the other people at the table at least. Furies are a small evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-17-2023, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:02:18-07:00","id":1515358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515357#post1515357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Save the earth plot seems more relevant now. It takes a war on for europeans to get somewhat serious about replacing fossil fuels, and even then it's just an economic incentive. .<br /> <br /> Yeah, furries are gross. Any kind of sexual act that isn't for the purpose of recreation should really earn you the death penalty in my humble eyes, but the WoD gameline has always been more a toolbox than a story (metaplot be damned) . Most characters in rollplaying games can do everything a human can and more, so unless the game specifically rules it out there's no mechanism to stop your character from committing acts of heinous sadism, beyond the actions of the other people at the table at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems needlessly hostile and also kind of odd given the prior editions' lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furies are a small evil. </div> </div> </div>Freudian slip? (^VVVVVV^)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:04:17-07:00","id":1515359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515355#post1515355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The MO seems to be &quot;Vampire was the most popular, so make everything look like Vampire to maximize monetization&quot;, with a side of a large, scummy corporation not liking that the game loudly shouts that large, scummy corporations are inherently aligned with a malignant spiritual force that twists and sickens the universe. With Vampire, there's some insulation between the text and subtext condemning older orders that have grown corrupt, but Werewolf's text is &quot;this is bad, Rage against it!&quot;. As a result, corporate pushes a &quot;street&quot; focus that's completely unearned and not even remotely authentic, in addition to flattening the play styles out further, in order to distract from the original narrative. The Apocalypse has already happened, there's no reason to do more than just try to survive, certainly not trying to make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>A theory I have is what W5 actually wants to aim for isn't that you shouldn't make a difference and wanting to do that is a bad thing, it's just... Garou shouldn't because they're fundamentally bad. So when Garou do their werewolf-stuff while constantly getting tormented via Frenzy/Harano/Hauglosk the antidote/good version of this is simply... mundane human life. Anything a normal human as an environmental activist can do is much better than anything these volatile, crazy Garou can do. So the idea W5 is actually going for is that it isn't just the case that being a Garou sucks but Garou as a whole are bad at what they do (and overall their presence in the world is a net-negative) and that the best way for Gaia to be saved is for them to step aside and let humanity save itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:08:33-07:00","id":1515360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515328#post1515328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is that there isn't a current lead dev. That one that worked on H5 and W5 (and has stated started work on more) left because he had a better job lined up and timed for when development on W5 was supposed to be finished. There's basically just a committee at Paradox working off old developer notes, and whatever freedom they give Renegade (and maybe Onyx Path if Onyx Path makes more WoD5 books at some point, which you'd think Paradox would want because the ones Onyx Path has worked on are considered some top tier books for the line). There is no vision, because there's no experienced TTRPG developer at the top of the decision ladder anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the part that gets me. This is a problem endemic to the entire entertainment industry right now and I just Don't Get It. Several AAA companies have already crashed/burned all their audience goodwill do to death by committee and are confused why many of their games are tanking, Many hollywood franchises are in the same boat, and the problem seems to have spread to the TTRPG space as well.<br /> <br /> Why do companies with consistent documentation and proof of concept for how this turns out, over the course of the last decade at least, seem to blind to the obvious consequences of jumping on the &quot;Comittee&quot; knows best bandwagon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515328#post1515328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure most people would be plenty happy to be Disney with Star Wars right now. For all that their first five movies are divisive, even with the bomb that was Solo financially, those movies paid off everything Disney spent to get Star Wars from Lucas. Focusing on shows for the time being has actually put Star Wars in a great place, as they've been much better received, which is bringing in profits and rebuild fan trust/excitement while they take their time deciding how to move forward with any films.<br /> <br /> Sure, you'd rather have had five blockbusters with great reception and great profits than what happened, but a rough start that you're actually recovering from and regardless of Internet reviews you still made a ton of money off of (even if most of that just wrote off the cost of buying the rights in the first place) is a lot better than most TTRPG companies could hope for.</div> </div> </div> </div>The watch stats for andor would disagree with this and the last indiana jones film shows that disney lucas films studios have not learned their lesson at all. They also fired the lead writer that made mandalorian good in the first place.<br /> <br /> They aren't recovering and they haven't quite learned, they're just large enough that they don't understand the death spiral yet. They've also lost money consistently on the last few live action movies, not just solo, so they are rather financially strained right now(which is causing a lot of turnover and layoffs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515328#post1515328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end how we all feel bout W5's RPG books basically isn't going to matter to Paradox. What's going to matter is if they can start making high profit projects in other markets (like, you know, video games from the video game company); Bloodlines 2 can be divisive and never really reach the classic status as the first, but if it sells well, they can actually put a dent in al the red from buying the WW IPs and the long development cycle for BL2, they can make their investors happy, and attract more projects by proving that VtM/WoD is still a brand big enough to really carry a franchise of video games, some streaming shows, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>For bloodlines to &quot;sell well&quot; it'll have to sell enough copies to make up for the money they lost being in perpetual development hell. It's more likely that they'll lose money on that investment due to dev drama and resource mismanagement.<br /> <br /> And if what you said is accurate, then they're even More short sighted. The reason to buy an established IP in the first place is so that you A.) have a product already tested to have potential for popularity(less risk of investing in a new product that flops) and B.) have an initial contingent of fans capable of causing audience takeoff(it's well know most people don't try to invest in something new unless they see other people invested in it, so having an existing fanbase increases a product's ability to hit market appeal numbers &quot;quickly enough&quot; increases geometrically proportional to the initial fanbase).<br /> <br /> Changing core aspects of the IP to that piss off existing fans destroys both those positives, gives you nearly the same risks as creating a new IP from scratch, and even creates a Negative feedback loop of bad advertising thanks to disgruntled fans. This means the company spent an initial investment of money on an IP only to need to spend More money on advertising and marketing than if they made a new IP from scratch. It's not unrecoverable by any means, but <i>it Is</i> a complete failure of management and waste of investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:11:48-07:00","id":1515363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515357#post1515357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Save the earth plot seems more relevant now. It takes a war on for europeans to get somewhat serious about replacing fossil fuels, and even then it's just an economic incentive. .<br /> <br /> Yeah, furries are gross. Any kind of sexual act that isn't for the purpose of recreation should really earn you the death penalty in my humble eyes, but the WoD gameline has always been more a toolbox than a story (metaplot be damned) . Most characters in rollplaying games can do everything a human can and more, so unless the game specifically rules it out there's no mechanism to stop your character from committing acts of heinous sadism, beyond the actions of the other people at the table at least. Furies are a small evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean recreation or procreation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:14:16-07:00","id":1515364,"title":"","content":"I had an entire reply typed out with talking points, only to be flagged when I went back to edit grammar. I hate this new automated system.<br /> <br /> More on topic, does anyone have houserules already lined up from what they've heard? I wonder what hybrid mechanic systems STs are going to come up with looking over W5, given how V20.5 carved it's own niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:19:19-07:00","id":1515367,"title":"","content":"Overall I find that 5th edition's rather juvenile idea of personal horror is really just... how to say this... I feel like all the splats have become allegory for neurodivergence? The vampires suck shit (weakened powers), can't control themselves (messy crits), they feel persecuted by the MAN (SI) despite the fact that they are the man, and they can't organize a conspiracy to save their lives (new faction changes). <br /> Werewolves look like they're to lose everything that made them great, their higher purpose, and the setting just focuses on them being depressed and unable to control themselves. <br /> <br /> As someone mostly comfortable in his body, who can control himself, and who could possibly be argued to be at least half-matured emotionally, this just seems a bit.. iffy? I'm happy to play the occasional character with issues but forcing it upon me is just alienating. You can't force someone to relate to someone else. Earlier WoD went with a broad approach and the situations the characters found themselves were very applicable to ordinary people, it was real punk. Having to deal with messy criticals or your war form being only for murder just strikes me as emo noise. Like I'm not this bitter in real life, I'm the fool that cries to every half-sad film, but I feel all 5th edition attempts at emotional engagements are just falling completely flat on their face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T07:20:35-07:00","id":1515368,"title":"","content":"Procreation, sorry, It was meant to be tongue in cheek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T08:14:07-07:00","id":1515373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515364#post1515364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had an entire reply typed out with talking points, only to be flagged when I went back to edit grammar. I hate this new automated system.<br /> <br /> More on topic, does anyone have houserules already lined up from what they've heard? I wonder what hybrid mechanic systems STs are going to come up with looking over W5, given how V20.5 carved it's own niche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is somenthing that you could use in the W5 that justify not just making an alternate version in place of a fix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T08:14:20-07:00","id":1515374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515355#post1515355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> a large, scummy corporation not liking that the game loudly shouts that large, scummy corporations are inherently aligned with a malignant spiritual force that twists and sickens the universe. With Vampire, there's some insulation between the text and subtext condemning older orders that have grown corrupt, but Werewolf's text is &quot;this is bad, Rage against it!&quot;. As a result, corporate pushes a &quot;street&quot; focus that's completely unearned and not even remotely authentic, in addition to flattening the play styles out further, in order to distract from the original narrative. The Apocalypse has already happened, there's no reason to do more than just try to survive, certainly not trying to make a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, WOD5E was the byproduct of a corporate conspiracy by a wannabe Pentex. <br /> <br /> I mean, it's still bogus, and it can be checked in, like, 30 seconds by looking at Martin Ericsson and Justin Achilli's Twitter feeds, but at least it's original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T08:30:43-07:00","id":1515376,"title":"","content":"Black Dog Game Factory it is not tho' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <i>Yet</i>...<br /> <br /> *Dun dun duuuuuun*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T09:32:00-07:00","id":1515381,"title":"","content":"I have friends who are furry WTA fans; more power to them. I can see why &quot;you're a huge sexy* monster, yet you are forbidden from having sex with the other huge sexy* monsters&quot; would be a compelling and dark setting to them XD<br /> <br /> I think going out of your way to <u>not</u> court such a market is foolish. Crinos seems to have been made much smaller, much less 'virile' and powerful, much less viable to lounge about (and do lounging about things), and all these decisions add up to &quot;furries aren't welcome&quot;, and if you like money you should like furries. They spend luxury car money on basically anything that floats their boat.<br /> <br /> Right now the key markets WtA5e seems to be targeting are:<br /> <br /> - twitter users who buy into &quot;the old fans are just racist grognards&quot;<br /> - people who like shiny new things<br /> - Progressive Content Enjoyers who also don't follow the news or listen to indigenous people<br /> <br /> A faithful new edition would have had:<br /> <br /> - most of the fans of the old editions<br /> - wolf-liking furries<br /> - potentially all furries if you play up the other breeds<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say that I don't think it'll be a smash hit in its current form.<br /> <br /> *if that floats your boat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T09:55:15-07:00","id":1515386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515373#post1515373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is somenthing that you could use in the W5 that justify not just making an alternate version in place of a fix?</div> </div> </div> </div>What? I'm not sure what you're asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:04:01-07:00","id":1515392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515381#post1515381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have friends who are furry WTA fans; more power to them. I can see why &quot;you're a huge sexy* monster, yet you are forbidden from having sex with the other huge sexy* monsters&quot; would be a compelling and dark setting to them XD<br /> <br /> I think going out of your way to <u>not</u> court such a market is foolish. Crinos seems to have been made much smaller, much less 'virile' and powerful, much less viable to lounge about (and do lounging about things), and all these decisions add up to &quot;furries aren't welcome&quot;, and if you like money you should like furries. They spend luxury car money on basically anything that floats their boat.<br /> <br /> Right now the key markets WtA5e seems to be targeting are:<br /> <br /> - twitter users who buy into &quot;the old fans are just racist grognards&quot;<br /> - people who like shiny new things<br /> - Progressive Content Enjoyers who also don't follow the news or listen to indigenous people<br /> <br /> A faithful new edition would have had:<br /> <br /> - most of the fans of the old editions<br /> - wolf-liking furries<br /> - potentially all furries if you play up the other breeds<br /> <br /> Suffice it to say that I don't think it'll be a smash hit in its current form.<br /> <br /> *if that floats your boat</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a single line written by someone at ParaWolf against &quot;furry people&quot;, or in justification of &quot; Antifurry as a Design Principle&quot;, or is it yet another Forum Legend about Wod5, probably based on buried discussions of 10-20 years ago? \ud83d\ude03","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:22:40-07:00","id":1515399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515386#post1515386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What? I'm not sure what you're asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>SOrry, my english sucks sometimes, What I mean is, have something in W5 that you can use so you can just fix the rest? Because if don't, it's better you do an alternative W5 ignoring the official.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:38:58-07:00","id":1515401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515374#post1515374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome, WOD5E was the byproduct of a corporate conspiracy by a wannabe Pentex.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's still bogus, and it can be checked in, like, 30 seconds by looking at Martin Ericsson and Justin Achilli's Twitter feeds, but at least it's original.</div> </div> </div> </div>All signs point to this being a bland, paint by the numbers redo with very little else to it, with a character type that's so constrained in action that they can barely do what they used to be able to prior to the reimagination. A corporation handed down mandates based on shareholder demands about production to a contracted team, and the contracted team carries it out or gets canned. That's the world that WoD production is now in; I don't put it past the shareholders to avoid trying to do what WotC did when they saw that WotC could still largely get away with shit like significant price hikes on digital-only books and the possibility of microtransactions in the future. In fact, we can't be sure that the shareholders aren't the same ones that are at WotC, can we? Lots of corporations have a rather degenerate pool of folks sitting on boards and giving out funding.<br /> <br /> At least, Justin was very correct about one thing - we don't need Pentex as a singular antagonist in Werewolf. All corporations are Pentex. Pentex was just a mask of deniability that WW had to shield itself from lawsuits if the parodied parties got really angry about anything (they didn't seem to notice, old W:tA should have gone further in).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:43:26-07:00","id":1515402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515392#post1515392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there a single line written by someone at ParaWolf against &quot;furry people&quot;, or in justification of &quot; Antifurry as a Design Principle&quot;, or is it yet another Forum Legend about Wod5, probably based on buried discussions of 10-20 years ago? \ud83d\ude03</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my take on the images and rules presented in this thread - the Crinos is a lanky skinny-wolf, all the forms are way smaller, they're sinewy and lithe and tiny, and they've gotten rid of Metis, and <i>basically</i> gotten rid of Lupus, along with making it so that if you're in Crinos you are in Murder Rage Mode where you are guaranteed to Frenzy if you don't kill something.<br /> <br /> Essentially, they've made this impossible: <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/6/69/Fianna_-_W20_Core_Rulebook%2C_p._86.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20150324212335\" target=\"_blank\">latest (889\u00d71217) (nocookie.net)</a>\u200b<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1255_1687023748390_681\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1255\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1255\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1255&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> That, to me, feels like sacrificing a very lucrative market. Whether it has been done deliberately or accidentally is something we can't be sure of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T11:09:58-07:00","id":1515405,"title":"","content":"If someone was against furries the smartest PR move would be to not say anything about furries. <br /> <br /> And yeah, furries are a scale. There are 17 main breeds of Khajiit and I'd... No, we're never getting a game in Elyswere, so let's hold that thought. I do think there's appeal for a man in Glabro... oh, what ever am I saying on a public forum? <br /> <br /> <br /> I've never had a problem with the idea that Werewolves can turn into wolves, be attracted to wolves as wolves, and mate with wolves as wolves. I'd be a little scared if we were talking mantis, but wolves? Fine. <br /> <br /> Creature suit fetishes are a real head scratcher for me. But I suppose that's true for all fetishes that aren't yours. Modern Humans have always been weirder around sex than violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T14:41:07-07:00","id":1515419,"title":"","content":"I hope you mean modern as it, &quot;the rise of <i>Homo sapiens</i> that coincided with the decline of the other hominids,&quot; not modern as if this is something from the past century or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T16:10:01-07:00","id":1515427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515401#post1515401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All signs point to this being a bland, paint by the numbers redo with very little else to it, with a character type that's so constrained in action that they can barely do what they used to be able to prior to the reimagination. A corporation handed down mandates based on shareholder demands about production to a contracted team, and the contracted team carries it out or gets canned .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> creating bland redo of a beloved ip with no imagination or talent? Guys, I think it is wrong to say that parawolk is a wanabee pentex.<br /> <br /> It's clearly a weaver company by this point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T13:43:10-07:00","id":1515559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515357#post1515357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Save the earth plot seems more relevant now. It takes a war on for europeans to get somewhat serious about replacing fossil fuels, and even then it's just an economic incentive. .<br /> <br /> Yeah, furries are gross. Any kind of sexual act that isn't for the purpose of procreation should really earn you the death penalty in my humble eyes, but the WoD gameline has always been more a toolbox than a story (metaplot be damned) . Most characters in rollplaying games can do everything a human can and more, so unless the game specifically rules it out there's no mechanism to stop your character from committing acts of heinous sadism, beyond the actions of the other people at the table at least. Furies are a small evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Okay, this is one of the most flagged posts I've seen in a while. You've indicated that it was intended as a joke but a lot of people weren't in on it, so that's worth a warning.</b></span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:08:25-07:00","id":1515634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515381#post1515381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - twitter users who buy into &quot;the old fans are just racist grognards&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They tend to form a co dependant dynamic with the grognards which results in the two groups dumbing down the dialogue and create false binaries. It probably doesn't help that a lot if online social interaction is filtered those sort of platforms.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for w5 they've already sunk that ship anyway. The twitter throng are poorly disposed to game due to the photo gaffes and I doubt the white washing out at least 3 tribes and removing two more will go down well with the grognards<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:32:10-07:00","id":1515635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515634#post1515634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They tend to form a co dependant dynamic with the grognards which results in the two groups dumbing down the dialogue and create false binaries. It probably doesn't help that a lot if online social interaction is filtered those sort of platforms.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for w5 they've already sunk that ship anyway. The twitter throng are poorly disposed to game due to the photo gaffes and I doubt the white washing out at least 3 tribes and removing two more will go down well with the grognards<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you don't get a lot out of &quot;I don't like it because it's not the old WtA.&quot; vs &quot;I like it because it's not the old WtA.&quot;. The photo gaffes are bad and considering that only Tame Iti's face has been changed who knows what awaits us once the whole book comes out...<br /> <br /> But what's troubling for me is stuff like the Tribe Favors. So far we got:<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: +1 die to Technology and Science when you build or repair things.<br /> Hart Wardens: +1 die to Animal Ken and Survival plus to nature-related Craft.<br /> Ghost Council: +1 die to Investigation, Occult and Subterfgue when you reveal a secret.<br /> Black Furies: +1 die when you oppose or circumvent someone in a position of power.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem like they thought of a consistent pattern to what these Favors do which is strange since we're talking about something as bland as a bonus-die to a roll here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T03:14:58-07:00","id":1515642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515635#post1515635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Glass Walkers: +1 die to Technology and Science when you build or repair things.<br /> Hart Wardens: +1 die to Animal Ken and Survival plus to nature-related Craft.<br /> Ghost Council: +1 die to Investigation, Occult and Subterfgue when you reveal a secret.<br /> Black Furies: +1 die when you oppose or circumvent someone in a position of power.<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem like they thought of a consistent pattern to what these Favors do which is strange since we're talking about something as bland as a bonus-die to a roll here...</div> </div> </div> </div>Walkers and council look okay but wardens and Furies are a little odd. Nature related craft is ultimatly technology-sorry but nature doesn't make wicker baskets or hunting tools and the Furies rule doesn't clarify about the nature of the authority-for example anything from institutional corruption to betrayal is fair game here.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it youd get a bonus to betraying everyone to the wyrm. It also hits the same issue as v5's brujah compulsion as it mechanically leans towards them being insubordinate dipshits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-20-2023, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T03:45:43-07:00","id":1515644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515642#post1515642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Walkers and council look okay but wardens and Furies are a little odd. Nature related craft is ultimatly technology-sorry but nature doesn't make wicker baskets or hunting tools and the Furies rule doesn't clarify about the nature of the authority-for example anything from institutional corruption to betrayal is fair game here.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it youd get a bonus to betraying everyone to the wyrm. It also hits the same issue as v5's brujah compulsion as it mechanically leans towards them being insubordinate dipshits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me just list them both:<br /> Glass Walkers:<ul><li>+1 die to Technology and Science when you build or repair things.</li> <li>Only regenerate 1 WP next session if you destroy complex machinery.</li> </ul>Hart Wardens:<ul><li>+1 die to Animal Ken and Survival plus to nature-related Craft.</li> <li>Only regenerate 1 WP next session if someone under your hospitality comes to harm.</li> </ul>Ghost Council:<ul><li>+1 die to Investigation, Occult and Subterfgue when you reveal a secret.</li> <li>Only regenerate 1 WP next session if when you had the opportunity to satisfy your curiosity, you didn't take it.</li> </ul>Black Furies:<ul><li>+1 die when you oppose or circumvent someone in a position of power.\u200b</li> <li>Only regenerate 1 WP next session if you witness an act of injustice that you could've prevented but didn't.</li> </ul>With GW, I'd probably add analyzing to make up for not having three applicable skills. And considering how Frenzy works I'm still wondering if acts under Frenzy can trigger Bans (then avoiding the destruction of complex machinery becomes a bit more complicated). The GC-favor/ban pairing is a bit weird because the favor is about revealing secrets and then the ban is <i>really</i> pushing the idea that you better be all about revealing secrets. Also, this &quot;opportunity to satisfy your curiosity&quot; could become really bad if it gets abused by the ST. With HW I think nature-related Craft refers to creating stuff that conceals things you want to hide in a forest or making makeshift-weapons out of stuff you find in nature... but &quot;nature-related&quot; is a bit vague in what it exactly refers to. Compared to the others it's pretty easy to avoid the HW-Ban, though... just don't accept guests into your home. And BF... yeah, if the Favor already paints them as people who are rebellious, the Ban really pushes them to get involved in other people's business as long as it seems like there's an injustice about to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T06:49:19-07:00","id":1515655,"title":"","content":"With the BF ones, what happens when the character BECOMES someone in power? Is it just a position of power in a vacuum or does Gorgon negate the benefit if the Fury is the sept alpha? XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T07:04:36-07:00","id":1515662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515655#post1515655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the BF ones, what happens when the character BECOMES someone in power? Is it just a position of power in a vacuum or does Gorgon negate the benefit if the Fury is the sept alpha? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, have you considered this, though: Garou-Elders are bad and societal positions of power in the Garou-Nation are by association also bad... The same way Hunters with Drive in H5 will never be members of a hunter-org, the &quot;good young Garou&quot; you're playing in W5 will never be Garou-Elders or be in a position of power when it comes to the remnants of the Garou-Nation.<br /> <br /> It would be in line with H5 to go for that type of worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T07:11:03-07:00","id":1515663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515662#post1515662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, have you considered this, though: Garou-Elders are bad and societal positions of power in the Garou-Nation are by association also bad... The same way Hunters with Drive in H5 will never be members of a hunter-org, the &quot;good young Garou&quot; you're playing in W5 will never be Garou-Elders or be in a position of power when it comes to the remnants of the Garou-Nation.<br /> <br /> It would be in line with H5 to go for that type of worldbuilding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, now I'm just picturing a bunch of young garou passing the position of authority around like a hot potato XD<br /> <br /> Or, they will go the hipster route and leave if something becomes too structured, man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T07:27:19-07:00","id":1515666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515663#post1515663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, now I'm just picturing a bunch of young garou passing the position of authority around like a hot potato XD<br /> <br /> Or, they will go the hipster route and leave if something becomes too structured, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or one PC takes a position of power and all the &quot;young good Garou&quot; immediately accuse them of &quot;selling out&quot; XD ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T09:55:40-07:00","id":1515676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515655#post1515655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the BF ones, what happens when the character BECOMES someone in power? Is it just a position of power in a vacuum or does Gorgon negate the benefit if the Fury is the sept alpha? XD</div> </div> </div> </div>See the problem is you're thinking off what happens if a pc garou is successful and effective which isn't supposed to happen. Now get back to keeping it real on street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T10:19:28-07:00","id":1515678,"title":"","content":"It didn't make sense to blame Garou &quot;Elders&quot; anyway. They aren't Vampires, Werewolves only live up to 100+ years, most dying violently before they hit the halfway point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T11:18:11-07:00","id":1515680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515678#post1515678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't make sense to blame Garou &quot;Elders&quot; anyway. They aren't Vampires, Werewolves only live up to 100+ years, most dying violently before they hit the halfway point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they could have worked in an issue with ancestor-spirits. Of course, that would require them to acknowledge that ancestor-spirits exist and are a notably thing a la Ancestors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T13:43:39-07:00","id":1515688,"title":"","content":"Antipathy towards conservative Elders who are (at least partly) to blame for the problems you're grappling with is a feature of W20's themes, and to me it makes sense. You don't need to be 500 years old to be a jaded political animal. An &quot;Elder&quot; in their 40s, 50s or 60s could be as regressive as you like, and may well have most of their historic Glory gained through intersept warfare and winning Challenges.<br /> <br /> Garou live in a Might Makes Right society, for the most part. I steal your favourite blanket. You're annoyed. Well if you want it back you'll have to challenge me. Oh you challenged me? Well time to find out why I felt so comfortable being such a dick to you. And I get some Glory for my troubles too.<br /> <br /> No matter how you square it, most Elders of any vaguely mainstream Sept are at the very least neutral towards stuff like &quot;all but 2-3 Tribes are pro killing the elderly&quot;, &quot;someone being strong means they won the argument&quot;, &quot;tormenting and mistreating one of the Breeds is acceptable&quot;.<br /> <br /> And you know what? Good.<br /> <br /> A setting where you have a Nation's worth of Elders, mighty and powerful beings who reinforce all this vile shit but are also incredibly important in the fight against the Wyrm, where you are directly subordinate to people who represent a lot of what you need to fight, where your access to Rites and Renown and Rank is tied to how well liked you are by people who are, honestly, monsters, is a setting which is amazing for a punk theme, or any tale of young rebellion you want to tell.<br /> <br /> And I've barely scratched the surface there. It's really hard to get into how many regressive, counterproductive and awful views a typical WTA NPC has, because so many of them exist and so many of them are best inferred from what we're told are exceptions. Children of Gaia wouldn't be described as being uniquely X if X weren't unique - same goes for Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> W5 removes the Garou Nation, from what we've seen, and leaves you to your own devices. This is based on previews, but that's the consistent impression I've gotten. It's made the Litany non-bigoted, but it's also made the Litany irrelevant. So what are you rebelling against exactly? What is the cost of being too cool for school new kids who fight the power? What society are you a punk IN?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T13:55:37-07:00","id":1515689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515688#post1515688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W5 removes the Garou Nation, from what we've seen, and leaves you to your own devices. This is based on previews, but that's the consistent impression I've gotten. It's made the Litany non-bigoted, but it's also made the Litany irrelevant. So what are you rebelling against exactly? What is the cost of being too cool for school new kids who fight the power? What society are you a punk IN?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind that so far the tribes all seem perfectly fine being on their own and doing their own thing with no mention how they dealt with the Nation falling. It feels like there never WAS a Nation to begin with.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T14:40:49-07:00","id":1515690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515689#post1515689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nevermind that so far the tribes all seem perfectly fine being on their own and doing their own thing with no mention how they dealt with the Nation falling. It feels like there never WAS a Nation to begin with.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The 'tribes' are almost certainly closer to character classes rather than full fledged cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T14:42:10-07:00","id":1515691,"title":"","content":"I think there's also an issue with how the idea of &quot;updating&quot; the game for the 2020s wasn't well thought out (or at least is extremely muddled by mixing two completely different attempts at W5). The Elders of 2023 were the young punks of 1993 with the generational shifts implied.Garou culture might be more stable/consistent for a number of reasons, but actually making a version of WtA that's timely to today's audience instead of timely to any era's audience would require a very different approach that what can be inferred so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T15:08:19-07:00","id":1515695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515688#post1515688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antipathy towards conservative Elders who are (at least partly) to blame for the problems you're grappling with is a feature of W20's themes, and to me it makes sense. You don't need to be 500 years old to be a jaded political animal. An &quot;Elder&quot; in their 40s, 50s or 60s could be as regressive as you like, and may well have most of their historic Glory gained through intersept warfare and winning Challenges.<br /> <br /> Garou live in a Might Makes Right society, for the most part. I steal your favourite blanket. You're annoyed. Well if you want it back you'll have to challenge me. Oh you challenged me? Well time to find out why I felt so comfortable being such a dick to you. And I get some Glory for my troubles too.<br /> <br /> No matter how you square it, most Elders of any vaguely mainstream Sept are at the very least neutral towards stuff like &quot;all but 2-3 Tribes are pro killing the elderly&quot;, &quot;someone being strong means they won the argument&quot;, &quot;tormenting and mistreating one of the Breeds is acceptable&quot;.<br /> <br /> And you know what? Good.<br /> <br /> A setting where you have a Nation's worth of Elders, mighty and powerful beings who reinforce all this vile shit but are also incredibly important in the fight against the Wyrm, where you are directly subordinate to people who represent a lot of what you need to fight, where your access to Rites and Renown and Rank is tied to how well liked you are by people who are, honestly, monsters, is a setting which is amazing for a punk theme, or any tale of young rebellion you want to tell.<br /> <br /> And I've barely scratched the surface there. It's really hard to get into how many regressive, counterproductive and awful views a typical WTA NPC has, because so many of them exist and so many of them are best inferred from what we're told are exceptions. Children of Gaia wouldn't be described as being uniquely X if X weren't unique - same goes for Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> W5 removes the Garou Nation, from what we've seen, and leaves you to your own devices. This is based on previews, but that's the consistent impression I've gotten. It's made the Litany non-bigoted, but it's also made the Litany irrelevant. So what are you rebelling against exactly? What is the cost of being too cool for school new kids who fight the power? What society are you a punk IN?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...there's an entire section of the Litany your ignoring there but ok.<br /> <br /> And yes there are aspects to all the Tribes that are great as concepts to struggle against and for Garou as individuals to have nuanced takes on but it doesn't feel like that is what W5 is doing.<br /> <br /> But for myself? Trying to turn WtA into V5 where all Elders are irredeemably monsters is missing out on so many interesting story hooks and themes that a deeper read such as we got in Revised...and partly in W20..allows.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-20-2023, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T15:17:50-07:00","id":1515696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515691#post1515691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's also an issue with how the idea of &quot;updating&quot; the game for the 2020s wasn't well thought out (or at least is extremely muddled by mixing two completely different attempts at W5). The Elders of 2023 were the young punks of 1993 with the generational shifts implied.Garou culture might be more stable/consistent for a number of reasons, but actually making a version of WtA that's timely to today's audience instead of timely to any era's audience would require a very different approach that what can be inferred so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> <br /> It's like all the folks who scream that the Garou committed Genocide against the Fera and therefore all current Garou are guilty of that crime. Yes, they did 15,000 years or more ago.<br /> <br /> Whereas my RL family did the same less than 200 years ago and noone, even the people's who were most effected, are asking for me to be flayed alive.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I do some small acts of recompense, far less than some Garou have done in Revised but I don't have the power to make it right and neither do the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T02:19:21-07:00","id":1515728,"title":"","content":"Something I remembered and which is another indicator of how rushed the development of W5 seemed to be is this section from the Tribes-dev-blog-post from last October:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tribe also imparts special spiritually mandated benefits and restrictions \u2014 a favor and a ban, something with which the werewolf gains proficiency from their spirit patron as well as a vow to uphold a certain way of life or attitude. For example, as a favor, Shadow Lords can conscript Stormcrow spirits to aid them, while, as a ban, the Galestalkers must partake of fresh kill daily, all based on the primal urges of their Patron Spirits. </div> </div> </div>This section is specifically talking about Favor and Bans and yet... now we know that all the Favors are a die-bonus to certain skills/actions. That means even last October they hadn't yet nailed down how Tribe Favors work. It certainly would explain the inconsistency since they were still developing the idea of how to handle Favor/Bans and were just rushing things after October to meet the January deadline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T02:33:22-07:00","id":1515729,"title":"","content":"Maybe that -do not suffer others to tend your sickness- shtick was invented precisely for the purpose of killing overly conservative elders... <br /> Well, no, it isn't, but it's a fun thought. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 'tribes' are almost certainly closer to character classes rather than full fledged cultures. </div> </div> </div> Didn't they overtly say that? They wanted culture neutral tribes. <br /> <br /> And yes, 5th edition is very <i>gamey</i>. You frenzy is you don't murder someone in crinos, vampires only fill their hunger when they kill someone, it's as if there's an invisible arbiter looking at bolean checkboxes ready to confirm deaths and offer rewards or punishments. Did you get a hit marker or a kill notification? Are we playing an arcade shooter or reading a webnovel with a system? Celerity 3 in V5 has two options in the corebook: Teleporting right next to an enemy to attack them or teleporting anywhere except for right next to an enemy... That's an arcade game choice, not something you want from a pen and paper rollplaying game where creativity and verismilitude are highly valued. (yeah, to an extent, Gifts being so specific is a little more arcade-like, but as they're spirit tricks it makes sense. vampire never had anything like that) <br /> <br /> It's just a dumb game in their minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T02:45:27-07:00","id":1515731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515728#post1515728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I remembered and which is another indicator of how rushed the development of W5 seemed to be is this section from the Tribes-dev-blog-post from last October:<br /> <br /> This section is specifically talking about Favor and Bans and yet... now we know that all the Favors are a die-bonus to certain skills/actions. That means even last October they hadn't yet nailed down how Tribe Favors work. It certainly would explain the inconsistency since they were still developing the idea of how to handle Favor/Bans and were just rushing things after October to meet the January deadline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they are even more out of wack than the current 4 indicate....it would be kinda funny if some get very circumstantial +s to rolls and others get to summon Spirit Companions and have no minuses as long as their mousetraps go off.<br /> <br /> &quot; Wait why are 90% of the people playing Shadow Lords?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T02:49:47-07:00","id":1515733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514964-garou-forms-plus-frenzy-rules-w5-preview?p=1515731#post1515731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot; Wait why are 90% of the people playing Shadow Lords?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sinse SL are only Garou who are -relatively- cool? Altough Rustovich slayed 6 their elders, so... no, not that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T03:37:18-07:00","id":1515735,"title":"","content":"Would\u2019ve been neat if all Tribal favors were structured as something like \u201cSummon a spirit of the Patron\u2019s brood, which can do one of the following on your behalf; fight alongside you, act as a temporary Fetish, or use a Tribal Gift of appropriate Rank.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T12:00:47-07:00","id":1515769,"title":"","content":"I kinda like the Forsaken 2e model, even if I wouldn't copy it directly, because it does a lot more to communicate what the Tribes are about, and actualize it in play. The core of each WtF 2e Tribe is preferred prey (because it focuses on wolves-as-hunters as guiding theme). A common (as in every pack basically needs at least one werewolf with it) rite is the Sacred Hunt. The Tribes provide a unique bonus to the Sacred hunt if lead by a member of that Tribe, and the prey is their favored prey. The Bone Shadow's favored prey is spirits, so when they lead the Sacred Hunt, their entire pack gets better at fighting spirits so they can attack that specific prey.<br /> <br /> I like the setup because it's far more engaging than just some dice bonuses, but it's also a lot easier for players and PCs to rely on than things like calling on a spirit to come help you out (in a fashion that doesn't just come down to that being a flavor of dice bonus). The idea of making sure that the Tribes are actually good at what they say they're supposed to be good at in same fashion is the main ideal, and it should be mixed with some common aspect of werewolf existence to help highlight their pack-nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}